{"chunk_id": "17096cb8a796", "text": "Drona tests his royal pupils with a famous lesson in focus: each prince must shoot the head of a bird placed on a tree. Yudhishthira, Duryodhana, and the others fail because they describe everything they see\u2014the tree, their teacher, their companions\u2014revealing scattered attention. Only Arjuna says he sees nothing but the bird, and even more precisely, only its head. Pleased, Drona orders him to shoot, and Arjuna instantly severs the bird\u2019s head. Later, while bathing in the Ganga, Drona is seized by an alligator and calls for help; Arjuna alone reacts instantly, killing the creature with arrows. Convinced of Arjuna\u2019s unmatched skill and discipline, Drona grants him the devastating Brahmasira weapon and prophesies that no archer will surpass him. The section establishes Arjuna\u2019s extraordinary focus and his special bond with his teacher.\nDrona tests his pupils\u2019 focus; only Arjuna succeeds, later saving Drona from a crocodile and receiving the devastating Brahmasira weapon.\nThemes: focused discipline, teacher and disciple, martial excellence, divine weapons, recognition of Arjuna", "vector": [-0.021952055394649506, -0.006517434027045965, -0.0048596663400530815, 0.005187209229916334, 0.008950609713792801, 0.02101621776819229, -0.025601817294955254, -0.01020730473101139, -0.02538791298866272, -0.025267591699957848, 0.005337611306458712, 0.016818322241306305, 0.010762122459709644, 0.008342315442860126, 0.011651166714727879, 0.011296886019408703, 0.04377041757106781, -0.02024081163108349, 0.023222118616104126, -0.020000167191028595, -0.014251455664634705, -0.010641800239682198, -0.0017079019453376532, 0.01782100461423397, 0.000818021537270397, 0.009645802900195122, 0.0042146071791648865, -0.027005573734641075, 0.0015892512165009975, -0.013048237189650536, 0.005835610441863537, 0.007607015315443277, -0.000871497904881835, -0.013021498918533325, -0.02291462942957878, 0.007840974256396294, -0.0060862805694341